// Encoder-roundtrip fuzz (deterministic, seeded): the oracle's fuzz
// harness generates twelve small valid-by-construction protocol
// variants inside the sealed vocabulary. Auxiliary event counts and payload
// classes, challenge spaces/dependency sets, domains, labels, and trailing
// proof layout vary around one exactly closed Schnorr shape. It emits each
// variant twice, as PIR text and as the protocol dict the oracle identifies.
// The gates:
//   1. every variant seals (valid-by-construction is real, not
//      assumed);
//   2. the sealed artifact is parse -> print -> parse stable
//      (re-reading the printed module reproduces it byte-for-byte);
//   3. the sealed identities equal the oracle's, in order — encode
//      determinism across both implementations on inputs nobody
//      hand-picked (the hand-written twins pin known points; this
//      pins a seeded neighborhood around them).
// The seed is fixed (oracle/fuzz.py SEED), so a failure is
// reproducible and a nondeterministic map iteration on either side
// breaks the byte diff first.
// REQUIRES: uv
// RUN: %uv python -m oracle.fuzz mlir > %t.gen.mlir
// RUN: zkc-opt %pir-seal-full %t.gen.mlir -o %t.sealed
// RUN: zkc-opt %t.sealed -o %t.reprint
// RUN: diff %t.sealed %t.reprint
// RUN: grep -o 'id "[0-9a-f]*"' %t.sealed > %t.got.ids
// RUN: %uv python -m oracle.fuzz ids > %t.want.ids
// RUN: diff %t.got.ids %t.want.ids
